  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 214 AM EDT Tue Oct 6 2026\n\n- Mostly Dry Conditions into the Weekend\n\nSouthwest flow today will bring breezy winds along with some\nslight chances (20 percent) for light rain mainly along and north\nof U-10 this morning. Dry air may limit this activity to\nsprinkles. A cold front then moves through tonight and may bring\nadditional light showers. As mentioned in the previous discussion\nmost of the lift will be north of the area along with the better\nmoisture, therefore most are expected to stay dry.\n\nNorthwest flow returns behind the front and continues until\nheights begin to rise for the weekend. There is a potential for\nfrost Thursday night into Friday morning again toward the US-10\ncorridor. Otherwise warmer temperatures are expected through the\nweek with highs in the 60s and 70s and lows in the 40s to 50s.",
